  o Minor bugfixes (buffers):
    - When flushing a buffer to a socket, a pipe, or a TLS connection, skip
      past any empty chunks at the start of the buffer. Previously, an empty
      chunk ahead of the data would make us write nothing and stop, leaving
      the rest of the data stuck in the buffer for good. Such a chunk can
      appear when buf_move_all() adds data after an empty chunk at the end
      of a buffer, though we don't know of a way to make this happen to a
      buffer that Tor flushes. Bugfix on 0.3.3.1-alpha.
